# Playwright output. Both rules below were already here and both were untrue
# about a path each: `git` does not un-track what is already indexed, so
# `packages/prism/playwright-report/index.html` (524 KB) and
# `packages/prism/test-results/.last-run.json` stayed in the tree from the
# commit that added these very lines.
#
# What they carried is the point. The `.last-run.json` said
# `{"status": "passed"}` for a suite that cannot run in this checkout at all —
# the browsers are not installed, and every spec fails with
# `browserType.launch: Executable doesn't exist`. The report is the viewer
# without its `data/` directory, so it opens showing no tests rather than an
# error: "nothing ran" and "nothing was recorded" render identically.
#
# An artifact that states an outcome is worse than no artifact. It answers the
# question without having done the work, and it answers it in the affirmative.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Misc
*.tgz
*.map.gz
